  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "dcdb6b23-2a0f-4c91-862f-c8d83ade0532",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1936,
        1520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Email daily operations briefs with Google Sheets, Supabase, and Claude\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow has two related automation paths: a scheduled daily operations brief process and a client signup process. Each morning it retrieves active clients from Supabase, loops through them, reads their revenue data from Google Sheets, analyzes anomalies, asks Claude to draft a brief, emails it, and logs the result back to Supabase. Separately, a signup webhook validates new client submissions, creates the client record, returns an HTTP response, and sends a welcome email on success.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure Supabase credentials and verify the active clients, client creation, and brief logging table/query settings.\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and ensure each client record contains the sheet details needed by the revenue-reading node.\n- Configure the Anthropic Claude HTTP request with a valid API key, model, headers, and prompt/body format.\n- Set up email sending credentials for both the daily operations brief and welcome email nodes.\n- Confirm the daily schedule time zone for the 07:00 trigger and activate the signup webhook URL in the calling application.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can adjust the daily schedule, the revenue anomaly logic, Claude prompt, email templates, recipient fields, and signup validation rules to match your operating process."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c4bbfabc-99e3-4d25-a33b-03438372e7ca",
